  "summary": "Five Euclid DR1 papers document the processing and calibration chains, with performance checked against requirements, ahead of scientific exploitation of the release.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the instrument-level processing and calibration underlying Euclid DR1. The papers describe NISP near-infrared processing and data products, NIR astrometric calibration with distortion modelling, quality control and residuals against Gaia DR3 reaching 30 mas, and SIR spectroscopic calibration that models the focal plane globally to meet wavelength and flux requirements. Ground-based optical imaging over about 2500 deg2 supplies colours, with photometric stability and depth validated for photo-z and PSF calibration. An overarching paper reviews the calibration plan, its implementation and performance against requirements, including corrections for flux, astrometry, PSF, shear and wavelength. The new element is the documented performance of these chains at DR1 scale; the items present pipelines and validation, not cosmological constraints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
